arm64: dts: h713: hy200-qz713df-a1: crust as the ARISC firmware, the display MIPS restart on

The HY300PRO-G-EU (this board, stock firmware projector05061226) gets the
HY310's ARISC path: crust, built for this board (crust
h713_hy200_qz713df_a1_sr_defconfig, board id 3), loaded as
hy200-qz713df-a1-crust.bin, the name release/build-all.sh installs it
under. Its stock tree agrees with the HY310's on what crust drives and
reads (power key PL4, the IR receiver, the LEDs PL0/PL1), and the DRAM
words crust uses are the same at this variant's 792 MHz.

The display MIPS node is no longer switched off here: on 03.10.2026 a
reload on this board through the old test bench ended black (doku/138),
before the restart driver (0231) and its TV top step (0239) existed; the
test of the driver on this board is what this tree is for. The other
variant of the board (projector09220931, 624 MHz) has no crust build yet
and would find no firmware under this name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts    | 15 ++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
index 62c4d41..f79d8ba 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
@@ -41,14 +41,15 @@
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
-/* The vendor ARISC image, as before: crust has run on the HY310 only. */
+/*
+ * crust, our ARISC firmware, as on the HY310: the board's stock tree agrees
+ * with the HY310's on the power key, the IR receiver and the LEDs, and the
+ * DRAM words crust uses are the HY310's (crust h713_hy200_qz713df_a1_sr).
+ * Built for the variant projector05061226 only (792 MHz); the image of the
+ * other variant has no crust yet and would find no firmware here.
+ */
 &arisc {
-	firmware-name = "h713-arisc.bin", "hy310-edid.bin";
-};
-
-/* The display MIPS restart is measured on the HY310 only. */
-&mips {
-	status = "disabled";
+	firmware-name = "hy200-qz713df-a1-crust.bin", "hy310-edid.bin";
 };
 
 /* PB5 stays the dtsi's hog here, not the board manager's (see above). */
